      "title": "Bonfire night maple bacon \u2018baked\u2019 beans",
      "content_html": "<h1 style=\"text-align:center;font-family:sans-serif;\">Bonfire night maple bacon \u2018baked\u2019 beans</h1>\n        <br>\n        <img src=\"https://www.strangerfoods.org/images/bonfire-night-maple-bacon-baked-beans.webp\" style=\"text-align:center;\"/>\n        <br>\n        <p style=\"font-family:sans-serif;>This makes a big batch, but it freezes really well and can be popped in the microwave to defrost and heat almost as quickly as taking a can of beans out of the pantry. Delicious piled into jacket potatoes and topped with cheese, or just serve on toast.</p>",
      "image": "https://www.strangerfoods.org/images/bonfire-night-maple-bacon-baked-beans.webp",
      "date_published": "2026-08-15T00:00:00+00:00Z",
      "language": "en"
    },
